# Our Little Universe: Progress

_Last updated: 2026-11-16_

A private couple website: one **admin** manages the space, one **user** gets a cozy place to check in, write, and (soon) chat, play and collect memories.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Backend | Laravel 13 (PHP 8.3+), MySQL |
| Frontend | React 19 + TypeScript (`.tsx`) via **Inertia 3** (pages live inside Laravel in `resources/js`) |
| Auth | **Custom session auth** (no Fortify, no Sanctum, no Laravel `Auth` guard) |
| Styling | Plain CSS with variables (`resources/css/olu*.css`), minimal on purpose; real design comes later |
| Realtime (planned) | Laravel Reverb + Laravel Echo (pure Laravel, no Node server) |

The project began from the Laravel React starter kit. Its starter tooling (Vite, Wayfinder, etc.) is left untouched. Fortify was not present in this install, so nothing had to be removed.

## Core design rules (from the concept doc)

- **Private by default.** Check-ins and journal entries carry a `visibility` of `private` or `shared`.
- **No admin bypass.** The admin sees only what she marks as shared.
- **Enforced in the backend.** Every query is scoped to the owner (`ownedBy` scopes). Non-owners get a 404, so existence is never revealed.
- **No pressure.** No streaks, no missed-day messaging, and gamification can be switched off in settings.
- **Safe notifications.** Previews default to off.

