## Known notes

- Her timezone defaults to `UTC`, so she should set the right one in Settings → Profile for "today" to be correct.
- Theme can flash briefly on first paint. A tiny inline script in the root Blade view can fix that during polish.
- Login throttling lives in `AuthController`, so the `login` limiter in `AppServiceProvider` can be removed.

## Next up: Slice 3, realtime chat

- Pure Laravel with **Reverb** and Echo, one private channel for the two participants.
- Messenger-style bubbles, typing indicator, "Seen", edit, unsend, and remove-from-my-view.
- A `messages` table with `sender_id`, `recipient_id`, `body`, `read_at`, `edited_at`, and per-side removal timestamps.
- Unread dot (not a count) on the sidebar.
- Echo's private-channel auth must be wired to our `ResolveSessionUser` middleware.
- Scheduled messages and open-when letters move to the Phase 3 letters feature.

---

## Slice 3: Realtime chat (done)

**Run extra:** `php artisan reverb:start --debug` (third terminal). Restart `npm run dev` after any `VITE_REVERB_*` change.

**Routes** (all behind `auth.session`)

| Method | URI | Action |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/chat` | `ChatController@index` (page, marks partner's messages read) |
| GET | `/chat/status` | `status` (channel name + unread flag, used by the sidebar dot) |
| GET | `/chat/messages?before=` | `older` (pagination) |
| POST | `/chat/messages` | `store` |
| POST | `/chat/read` | `read` |
| PATCH | `/chat/messages/{message}` | `update` (sender only) |
| DELETE | `/chat/messages/{message}` | `unsend` (sender only, wipes the text) |
| POST | `/chat/messages/{message}/remove` | `remove` (hide from my view only) |

**Backend:** `messages` migration (`..._000010`), `Message` model (`between`, `visibleTo`, `toPayload`, `channelFor`), `ChatUpdated` event (`ShouldBroadcastNow`, so no queue worker; one event for sent/edited/unsent/read), `ChatController`, channel `chat.{a}.{b}` in `routes/channels.php` (only the two participants).

**Frontend:** `lib/http.ts` (fetch + XSRF), `lib/echo.ts` (single shared Echo instance, reset on logout), `components/chat-dot.tsx` (unread dot in the sidebar), `pages/chat/index.tsx`. Chat styles are in `olu-features.css`.

**Notes**
- Partner = the other active user (assumes exactly two accounts).
- Typing indicator uses Echo whispers (client events), nothing stored.
- Echo must stay a single instance: recreating it from the sidebar and the page at the same time killed the subscription.

---

## Slice 4: Calendar (done)

- Routes: `resource /calendar` (param `event`, no show). Owner edits; the other person sees only `shared` events; non-owners get 404.
- Backend: `calendar_events` migration (`..._000011`), `EventType` enum, `CalendarEvent` model (`visibleTo`, `occurrenceInMonth`, `nextOccurrence`, yearly repeats, Feb 29 handled), `CalendarEventRequest`, `CalendarController`.
- Frontend: `lib/calendar.ts`, `components/calendar-form.tsx`, `pages/calendar/{index,create,edit}.tsx`. Home shows the next special date tile (`HomeController` computes it in her timezone).

## Slice 5: Admin content manager (done)

- `content_items` (one table, `kind` = question | compliment | comfort, `body`, `is_active`), migration `..._000012`, `ContentKind` enum, `ContentItem` model (`dailyPick` = same pick all day, `randomBody`), `ContentSeeder` (starter content, run with `php artisan db:seed --class=ContentSeeder`).
- Admin: `/admin/content` (tabs, add, edit, hide, delete), `role:admin` only, touches only this table.
- Her side: Home shows the daily compliment ("Another one" button) and question of the day; `/comfort` page; JSON `GET /content/random/{kind}`.
- Answering the daily question is not built yet (comes with the Phase 3 shared questions).